-- title:
--   From HTo G
-- statement:
--   **The family hypotheses imply the complete from-H-to-G comparison.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a good successor strategy and let $F$ be an indexed polynomial family. Assume
--
--   $$
--   0\le\gamma\le1,\qquad0\le\zeta\le1,\qquad d\le q.
--   $$
--
--   Assume that $F$ is consistent with the point measurement with error $\zeta$, strongly self-consistent with the strategy state with error $\zeta$, and satisfies the slice-boundedness input with error $\zeta$. For any errors $\varepsilon,\delta$ used in the goodness hypothesis and any $k\in\mathbb N$, the resulting `FromHToGStatement` gives
--
--   $$
--   \left|M_{\mathrm{all}}(S,\operatorname{state}(S),F,k)-T_{\mathrm{tail}}(\operatorname{state}(S),F,k)\right|
--   \le46k^2m\left(\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+(d/q)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The displayed right-hand side is the exact `fromHToGError` envelope. This theorem is the public strategy-state wrapper used by the Bernoulli-tail completeness theorem and obtains the G-hat and half-sandwich hypotheses needed by the preceding comparison result.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Bernoulli/FromHToG.lean#L111-L139

